; Guards 20/F042: the GAP9 half-precision builtins. float16 max/min/sqrt are
; fmax.h/fmin.h/fsqrt.h; the packed v2h forms are one scalar .h operation per
; lane; the bfloat16 forms (passed as their i16 / i32 bits) are computed on
; f32 in the GPRs with integer shifts and round-to-nearest-even, never through
; the libcall __truncsfbf2 (missing from GAP9's libgcc). max/min keep the
; instruction (fmax/fmin) even with a NaN constant operand, so the result is
; the instruction's canonical NaN rather than a folded operand.

